  "prediction_registered_before_the_run": "Cutting the genome at random destroys boundaries and creates adjacencies constantly, so the first two claims will fire at most control rearrangements, and naming the recipient gene will land near the 90% that naming a target already reaches at matched windows. What should separate the published rearrangements is which gene, and nothing else - if it does not, the node model has failed its sharpest test.",
